# Dadix

Two products share `app/src`: Web (`app/`, :3000/:6127) and Desktop (`dadix-desktop/` + `crates/dadix-core`).

Desktop path only: `app/src` → `bridge/callApi.ts` → `lib/dadix.ts` → `dadix_*` → `dadix-core` → SQLite `.dadix` / DuckDB RAM.

Before structural work read `docs/README.md` and `AGENTS.md`.

- Project logic in `dadix-core`. Tauri commands stay thin.
- Never import `@tauri-apps/api` from `app/src`. Use `desktopShell.ts` / `window.__dadix*`.
- Do not build a second desktop workspace UI. Ignore `dadix-desktop/src/components/workspace/`.
- Product proof is built `Dadix.app`, not `tauri dev`. Keep `frontendDist: ../dist`.
- No secrets in `.dadix`. No auto `*.duckdb`. No bind-all + DESCRIBE on open.
- macOS: hide only the three traffic-light buttons; never the superview; no `trafficLightPosition`; no native titlebar `setFrame` to 44px.
- `ViewsSwitch` must call `useLanguage()`. Open URL via `openExternalUrl`, not `window.open`.
